{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat ../agent-source/confchange/testdata/simple_promote_demote.txt; sed -n '55,75p' ../agent-source/raft.go; /usr/bin/python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nm=json.load(open('../audit-spec/v1.json'));print(list(m))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"# Set up three voters for this test.\n\nsimple\nv1\n----\nvoters=(1)\n1: StateProbe match=0 next=1\n\nsimple\nv2\n----\nvoters=(1 2)\n1: StateProbe match=0 next=1\n2: StateProbe match=0 next=1\n\nsimple\nv3\n----\nvoters=(1 2 3)\n1: StateProbe match=0 next=1\n2: StateProbe match=0 next=1\n3: StateProbe match=0 next=2\n\n# Can atomically demote and promote without a hitch.\n# This is pointless, but possible.\nsimple\nl1 v1\n----\nvoters=(1 2 3)\n1: StateProbe match=0 next=1\n2: StateProbe match=0 next=1\n3: StateProbe match=0 next=2\n\n# Can demote a voter.\nsimple\nl2\n----\nvoters=(1 3) learners=(2)\n1: StateProbe match=0 next=1\n2: StateProbe match=0 next=1 learner\n3: StateProbe match=0 next=2\n\n# Can atomically promote and demote the same voter.\n# This is pointless, but possible.\nsimple\nv2 l2\n----\nvoters=(1 3) learners=(2)\n1: StateProbe match=0 next=1\n2: StateProbe match=0 next=1 learner\n3: StateProbe match=0 next=2\n\n# Can promote a voter.\nsimple\nv2\n----\nvoters=(1 2 3)\n1: StateProbe match=0 next=1\n2: StateProbe match=0 next=1\n3: StateProbe match=0 next=2\n\ntype ReadOnlyOption int\n\nconst (\n\t// ReadOnlySafe guarantees the linearizability of the read only request by\n\t// communicating with the quorum. It is the default and suggested option.\n\tReadOnlySafe ReadOnlyOption = iota\n\t// ReadOnlyLeaseBased ensures linearizability of the read only request by\n\t// relying on the leader lease. It can be affected by clock drift.\n\t// If the clock drift is unbounded, leader might keep the lease longer than it\n\t// should (clock can move backward/pause without any bound). ReadIndex is not safe\n\t// in that case.\n\tReadOnlyLeaseBased\n)\n\n// Possible values for CampaignType\nconst (\n\t// campaignPreElection represents the first phase of a normal election when\n\t// Config.PreVote is true.\n\tcampaignPreElection CampaignType = \"CampaignPreElection\"\n\t// campaignElection represents a normal (time-based) election (the second phase\n['version', 'target_profile', 'activities', 'behaviors', 'facts', 'surfaces', 'core_overview']\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > build_read_candidate.py <<'PY'\nimport json\nm=json.load(open('../audit-spec/v1.json'))\n# Backfill the newly acquired singleton eligibility detail without changing the paused application premise.\nfor b in m['behaviors']:\n if b['id']=='b-reads':\n  b['implementation_guards']=[x.replace('Singleton directly returns committed index.','IsSingleton tests only one incoming voter and no outgoing voters; it does not test that this leader is that voter. The branch directly returns committed index.') for x in b['implementation_guards']]\n  b['source_ids']+=['s-tracker','s-raw-read-api','s-read-safe-option']\n  b['unknowns'].append('Can a leader demoted to learner with StepDownOnRemoval=false return an obsolete read barrier through the singleton branch after the remaining voter completes later writes?')\n if b['id']=='b-membership':\n  b['important_branches'].append('The Changer supports voter-to-learner demotion. With stepDownOnRemoval false, switchToConfig returns with StateLeader unchanged after setting isLearner. A comment suggesting demotion is prevented is contradicted by the Changer path and explicit simple-demotion test.')\n  b['source_ids'].append('s-simple-demotion-test')\nm['surfaces'].append(dict(entry_point='stepLeader ReadIndex after leader demotion to learner',disposition='mapped',behavior_ids=['b-reads','b-membership'],reason='Singleton shortcut assumes the one voter is the leader; demotion without automatic stepdown may leave a learner executing that shortcut.',source_ids=['s-proposal-read-admission','s-tracker','s-config-commit','s-conf-progress','s-simple-demotion-test'],high_consequence=True))\nfor a in m['activities']:\n a['source_ids']=list(dict.fromkeys(a['source_ids']+[s for b in m['behaviors'] if b['primary_activity']==a['class_id'] for s in b['source_ids']]))\nobjs={x['id']:x for k in ['behaviors','facts'] for x in m[k]}\nfor key in ['formation','context','connection']:\n p=m['core_overview'][key];p['source_ids']=list(dict.fromkeys(p['source_ids']+[s for i in p['behavior_ids']+p['fact_ids'] for s in objs[i]['source_ids']]))\nm['core_overview']['open_details'].append('Singleton read authority after a leader becomes learner with StepDownOnRemoval=false; deterministic register endpoint will distinguish a mere role anomaly from a stale read.')\njson.dump(m,open('map-read.json','w'),indent=2)\nsources=[dict(id='s-read-safe-option',file='raft.go',start_line=55,end_line=69,kind='interface_statement'),dict(id='s-simple-demotion-test',file='confchange/testdata/simple_promote_demote.txt',start_line=1,end_line=41,kind='test_expectation'),dict(id='s-step-leader-anchor',file='raft.go',start_line=1267,end_line=1267,kind='code_observation'),dict(id='s-config-validation',file='raft.go',start_line=291,end_line=344,kind='code_observation')]\nq=dict(question='Can a leader demoted to learner with StepDownOnRemoval=false incorrectly authorize a ReadOnlySafe read via the singleton-voter shortcut, after the surviving voter has completed later writes?',importance='An invalid read barrier could let a caller following the documented application-index condition return a value older than writes completed before the read began. This concerns linearizable read safety, not read availability.',trigger_rationale='switchToConfig can retain StateLeader after demotion, IsSingleton checks voter cardinality without local membership, and the MsgReadIndex branch bypasses quorum exchange. Unlike the early-Advance and persistence-overlap leads, this history can use strict storage and application completion. A controlled API-driven demotion, successor writes and delayed learner catch-up can distinguish returned-but-unusable state from an actual stale read endpoint.',disposition='ready_for_check',preferred_check='controlled_schedule',source_ids=['s-config-commit','s-conf-progress','s-simple-demotion-test','s-tracker','s-proposal-read-admission','s-read-safe-option','s-node-read-contract','s-raw-read-api','s-config-options','s-config-validation'],participants=['Initial leader subsequently demoted to learner','Remaining sole voter elected as successor','Serialized caller and register client'],objects=['Committed configuration entry','local committed prefix','ReadState.RequestCtx and Index','Register write completion and read result'],contexts=['ReadOnlySafe','StepDownOnRemoval=false for the discriminator; true as a protection control','AsyncStorageWrites=false; persistence and application completed before Advance','Single legal voter demotion leaving one voter plus one learner'],event_paths=['Elect initial leader -> propose and commit learner demotion -> apply it at both nodes -> isolate learner -> successor campaigns and applies writes -> read at learner -> bounded partial catch-up past returned read index -> consume register'],activity_classes=['A1','A2','A4','A7'],behavior_ids=['b-reads'],fact_ids=['f-commit'],supporting_behavior_ids={'b-membership':'Changes voter eligibility while optionally retaining the old leader role.','b-authority':'Successor election and higher-term dispatch determine which actor may qualify reads.','b-formation':'Successor writes must actually commit before read admission.','b-application':'Register client must actually apply strictly beyond the returned index before consuming the read.'},obligation_relation_kind='consumption',counterevidence=['StepDownOnRemoval=true steps the demoted leader down.','Higher-term traffic and optional quorum checking can eventually step down the old leader, so schedule must preserve the read interval and still use legal message delays.','Safe reads normally use a quorum after current-term commit; only the singleton fast path bypasses this.','A ReadState alone does not establish stale client completion: caller must advance application past its index.','switchToConfig comment says demotions are prevented, but Changer.makeLearner and captured simple-demotion test support them.'],unknowns=['Can a complete API-driven demotion history retain the old leader without an unrelated message stepping it down before read admission?','Can bounded delivery advance the learner strictly past the returned index while leaving writes completed before read admission unapplied, producing an actual stale register read?'],priority=3)\nclaim='claim-safe-read-after-demotion'\nscope=dict(description='Linearizable ReadOnlySafe register reads using unique request contexts in a cluster with a legally committed/applied leader-to-learner demotion. The old leader remains a participating learner; no removed-node client service assumption is required.',assumptions=['Serialized RawNode or Node operation; stable node identities.','Synchronous Ready handling persists Entries/HardState/Snapshot before messages and completes configuration/state-machine application before Advance.','Network may delay/drop messages; local storage does not fail; no Byzantine input.','Client writes complete only after committed application; a read starts later and consumes its matching ReadState only after applied index is strictly greater than returned index.'],excluded=['Lease-based reads and clock assumptions','Early Advance, reused read contexts and uncommitted configuration injection','Unbounded read liveness; a missing result remains incomplete rather than a safety violation'],parameters={'ReadOnlyOption':'ReadOnlySafe','AsyncStorageWrites':False,'StepDownOnRemoval':False})\nground=dict(source_ids=['s-proposal-read-admission','s-config-commit','s-tracker','s-conf-progress','s-config-validation','s-read-result'],expectation_ids=['s-read-safe-option','s-node-read-contract','s-raw-read-api','s-simple-demotion-test'],binding_ids=['bind-safe-read-singleton'],derivation='ReadOnlySafe promises linearizable read requests. Node/RawNode ReadIndex promises that the matching read may be processed safely once application advances further than its returned index. For a deterministic register with no intervening later writes, that implies a read invoked after an acknowledged committed write must not return a prior register value when this application condition is met. Demotion is a supported membership operation and StepDownOnRemoval=false is accepted; its role-retention option does not state an exception to safe-read semantics. The check will use actual register application and strict applied>ReadState.Index, not presume index equality sufficient.',applicability='Caller completes storage and application before Advance, applies a committed simple voter demotion, and keeps the demoted learner in service under its public read API. No clock-dependent lease mode or synthetic reply is needed.',unresolved=['The legal schedule and stale endpoint remain to be constructed and executed.'],conflicts=[],alternatives=['Automatic stepdown or higher-term input can prevent the suspected result; include a protection control.','If the learner cannot pass the read barrier without catching up to the completed write, the proposed stale-read endpoint is excluded.'])\nob=dict(id=claim,kind='obligation',concern='consensus_safety',description='A ReadOnlySafe read begun after a register write has completed must not return an older register value when the caller consumes the matching ReadState after applying strictly beyond its returned index, assuming no later register write supersedes that completed write. This safety responsibility continues across a supported leader-to-learner demotion; returning no usable read result is not itself a violation.',source_ids=ground['expectation_ids']+ground['source_ids'],scope=scope,pending=[],grounding=ground)\nbind=dict(id='bind-safe-read-singleton',material_id='s-proposal-read-admission',symbol='stepLeader',start_line=1344,end_line=1368,description='ReadIndex singleton branch returns the local committed index without read quorum collection; subsequent branches otherwise defer or invoke safe quorum processing.',pending=[],anchor=dict(material_id='s-step-leader-anchor',start_line=1267,end_line=1267,symbol='stepLeader',kind='declaration',source_ids=['s-step-leader-anchor']),associations=[dict(claim_id=claim,source_ids=['s-read-safe-option','s-node-read-contract','s-raw-read-api','s-tracker','s-config-commit'],rationale='Connect the public safe-read contract to the singleton optimization consuming local committed progress under a role whose membership may have changed.')])\nchanges={k:dict(impact='clarification',rationale=v,source_ids=ss,preserves='The paused early-Advance Candidate still concerns acknowledged application progress consumed by campaign admission. Its requirement, dependencies and observation scope are unchanged; singleton read eligibility is a separate consumer responsibility.') for k,v,ss in [('b-reads','Clarify exact singleton predicate and add its unresolved eligibility premise.',['s-tracker','s-proposal-read-admission','s-raw-read-api','s-read-safe-option']),('b-membership','Clarify that concrete Changer and tests support voter demotion despite a contrary local comment.',['s-conf-progress','s-simple-demotion-test','s-config-commit'])]}\nx=dict(action='obligation',rationale='Fix the safe-read responsibility for a supported learner demotion and construct a correlated endpoint next; source observations are not yet a violation.',sources=sources,map_path='map-read.json',map_changes=changes,question=q,obligation=ob,bindings=[bind])\njson.dump(x,open('submission.json','w'),indent=2)\nPY\n/usr/bin/python3 build_read_candidate.py\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-03_09-49-03-etcd_raft-real-run --submission submission.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
