on test support them.'],unknowns=['Can a complete API-driven demotion history retain the old leader without an unrelated message stepping it down before read admission?','Can bounded delivery advance the learner strictly past the returned index while leaving writes completed before read admission unapplied, producing an actual stale register read?'],priority=3)\nclaim='claim-safe-read-after-demotion'\nscope=dict(description='Linearizable ReadOnlySafe register reads using unique request contexts in a cluster with a legally committed/applied leader-to-learner demotion. The old leader remains a participating learner; no removed-node client service assumption is required.',assumptions=['Serialized RawNode or Node operation; stable node identities.','Synchronous Ready handling persists Entries/HardState/Snapshot before messages and completes configuration/state-machine application before Advance.','Network may delay/drop messages; local storage does not fail; no Byzantine input.','Client writes complete only after committed application; a read starts later and consumes its matching ReadState only after applied index is strictly greater than returned index.'],excluded=['Lease-based reads and clock assumptions','Early Advance, reused read contexts and uncommitted configuration injection','Unbounded read liveness; a missing result remains incomplete rather than a safety violation'],parameters={'ReadOnlyOption':'ReadOnlySafe','AsyncStorageWrites':False,'StepDownOnRemoval':False})\nground=dict(source_ids=['s-proposal-read-admission','s-config-commit','s-tracker','s-conf-progress','s-config-validation','s-read-result'],expectation_ids=['s-read-safe-option','s-node-read-contract','s-raw-read-api','s-simple-demotion-test'],binding_ids=['bind-safe-read-singleton'],derivation='ReadOnlySafe promises linearizable read requests. Node/RawNode ReadIndex promises that the matching read may be processed safely once application advances further than its returned index. For a deterministic register with no intervening later writes, that implies a read invoked after an acknowledged committed write must not return a prior register value when this application condition is met. Demotion is a supported membership operation and StepDownOnRemoval=false is accepted; its role-retention option does not state an exception to safe-read semantics. The check will use actual register application and strict applied>ReadState.Index, not presume index equality sufficient.',applicability='Caller completes storage and application before Advance, applies a committed simple voter demotion, and keeps the demoted learner in service under its public read API. No clock-dependent lease mode or synthetic reply is needed.',unresolved=['The legal schedule and stale endpoint remain to be constructed and executed.'],conflicts=[],alternatives=['Automatic stepdown or higher-term input can prevent the suspected result; include a protection control.','If the learner cannot pass the read barrier without catching up to the completed write, the proposed stale-read endpoint is excluded.'])\nob=dict(id=claim,kind='obligation',concern='consensus_safety',description='A ReadOnlySafe read begun after a register write has completed must not return an older register value when the caller consumes the matching ReadState after applying strictly beyond its returned index, assuming no later register write supersedes that completed write. This safety responsibility continues across a supported leader-to-learner demotion; returning no usable read result is not itself a violation.',source_ids=ground['expectation_ids']+ground['source_ids'],scope=scope,pending=[],grounding=ground)\nbind=dict(id='bind-safe-read-singleton',material_id='s-proposal-read-admission',symbol='stepLeader',start_line=1344,end_line=1368,description='ReadIndex singleton branch returns the local committed index without read quorum collection; subsequent branches otherwise defer or invoke safe quorum processing.',pending=[],anchor=dict(material_id='s-step-leader-anchor',start_line=1267,end_line=1267,symbol='stepLeader',kind='declaration',source_ids=['s-step-leader-anchor']),associations=[dict(claim_id=claim,source_ids=['s-read-safe-option','s-node-read-contract','s-raw-read-api','s-tracker','s-config-commit'],rationale='Connect the public safe-read contract to the singleton optimization consuming local committed progress under a role whose membership may have changed.')])\nchanges={k:dict(impact='clarification',rationale=v,source_ids=ss,preserves='The paused early-Advance Candidate still concerns acknowledged application progress consumed by campaign admission. Its requirement, dependencies and observation scope are unchanged; singleton read eligibility is a separate consumer responsibility.') for k,v,ss in [('b-reads','Clarify exact singleton predicate and add its unresolved eligibility premise.',['s-tracker','s-proposal-read-admission','s-raw-read-api','s-read-safe-option']),('b-membership','Clarify that concrete Changer and tests support voter demotion despite a contrary local comment.',['s-conf-progress','s-simple-demotion-test','s-config-commit'])]}\nx=dict(action='obligation',rationale='Fix the safe-read responsibility for a supported learner demotion and construct a correlated endpoint next; source observations are not yet a violation.',sources=sources,map_path='map-read.json',map_changes=changes,question=q,obligation=ob,bindings=[bind])\njson.dump(x,open('submission.json','w'),indent=2)\nPY\n/usr/bin/python3 build_read_candidate.py\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-03_09-49-03-etcd_raft-real-run --submission submission.json\"","aggregated_output":"{\"valid\": false, \"run_id\": \"aeb91e843ac444a88a3bbe1fc64e445d\", \"audit_spec_version\":